{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "progress_weighted_regret",
  "intent": "Make regret the dominant late-stage signal by scaling its weight with progress (0.20 + 0.45*progress, so 0.20 early -> 0.65 late), since the regret gap is most informative when few cities remain and the tour structure is crystallizing. Return penalty is also progress-gated (0.10*return_distance*progress) so it only activates near tour closure. Cluster density stays light to avoid overweighting features that are noisy in uniform/grid topologies. Distance remains the primary anchor for local coherence, matching the seed rule, with regret as the secondary ranking signal that prevents forced long jumps when a clearly closer next neighbor exists.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "progress"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    p = f['progress']\n    d = f['distance']\n    r = f['return_distance']\n    reg = f['regret']\n    den = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + (0.20 + 0.45 * p) * reg + 0.10 * r * p + 0.05 * den",
